From abdcdac966ba1a3edc250f8ed0740ffb302c145c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 16:31:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(manager): serve overtake-tool remote UIs (dedicated Tool
 tab + rev-gated poll)

Lets an overtake tool (component_type:"tool", which takes over the Move surface)
expose a browser remote UI the same way chain/synth modules can. Manager-only;
builds on the remote-UI infra from #118/#132:

- discover the active overtake tool via overtake_dsp:module_id and serve its
  web_ui.html under a dedicated Tool tab in the remote UI
- bridge the browser's param get/set through the existing overtake_dsp:-prefixed
  SHM path; seed initial values from the tool's overtake_dsp:state snapshot
- pop-out button for the Tool tab (matching the custom-UI pop-out from #132)
- rev-gate the tool poll: a cheap overtake_dsp:rui_poll digest (rev:on:tick:bpm)
  lets the manager skip the heavy overtake_dsp:state read unless the tool's
  content rev changed, pushing just the lightweight playhead while playing

No DSP/shim changes; fully generic with no module-specific assumptions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SccYnQe2WXaEwGhP1T7nuT
